                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Never knew this existed, found out it did when researching the old PS1 game \"LSD Dream Emulator\" that the creator of the game claims it was influenced by. (You can definitely see the influence!)\n\nFirst off, I find it an absolute shame that games like this go unknown. It's a rare little example of its type - most of the \"game\" here involves going through in story mode and finishing the game which is... uh, an interesting experience.\n\nI am enjoying myself late at night when it's relaxing and I have a loop game or somesuch playing in another window - it's fun to wander around and occasionally ask my wife what she thinks the meaning of, say, a dead blue lobster stuck underneath stained hospital bedsheets might signify. It's not really the kind of game that will absorb all of your attention or skill... it's more of a dreamlike experience of just wandering around and piecing things together. (Or not piecing them together if you prefer I guess!)\n\nCool little game/visual experience/whatever you want to call it. I wish more people knew about it.",
